          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అధికారం — adhikāraṁ — \"power; authority\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆ పని చేసే అధికారం అతనికి లేదు. ā pani cēsē adhikāraṁ ataniki lēdu. He has no authority to do that."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అధికారి, an officer, which you know, is the one who holds it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అధికారం (adhikāraṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit adhikāra, \"authority; government, rule, administration\" (Monier-Williams); అధికారి, an officer, is the same word."
            }
          ]
        },
